# Roll call and Tim: Gemini batch 2 (2026-10-03 v001).
[rollcall_open]
- Mornin' over the fence, folks. Sound off on the horn and let the captain know the line's workin'.
- Well now, looks like the dust is settlin'. Check in on your channels, neighbours, nice and orderly.
- Station's stretchin' its joints today. Give the pilot a toot on the comms so we know who's on deck.
- Hello the house! Radios are warm and runnin'. Sound off, crew, and let folks know your call sign.
- Sun's up over the solar banks. Roll call time, neighbours. Let's hear who's holdin' the watch.
- Quiet mornin' out here in the black. Tap your relays and let the captain know how to ring your bell.
- Roll call down the fence line. Make your check-in short, clean, and give the pilot your handle.

[rollcall_close]
- And that's the whole fence line accounted for. Give me a holler with {command} if you need an ear.
- Good crew, good neighbours. If you ever want some quiet porch talk, type {command} to flag me down.
- All square on the roster. Remember, neighbour, {command} fetches me right over if things get knotty.
- Looks like we're in fine fettle today. Just ring {command} when you want to lean on the fence a spell.
- Full deck, clean airlocks. Keep your wrenches handy, and type {command} whenever you need old Wilson.
- Roll call complete, pilot. If the chatter gets thick or you need a word, {command} brings me right over.
- Everyone's at their station. Have a peaceful shift out there, and punch in {command} if you need me.

[exchange trigger=any.tim]
Tim: Hear me out, Wilson: twin turbo-blowers on the air scrubber intake!
Wilson: Well now, Tim, breathable air don't need to arrive at eighty miles an hour.
Tim: But think of the cabin circulation, neighbour!

[exchange trigger=any.tim]
Tim: I just bypassed the rotor safety pins. We're gonna get twice the spin on this drill rig!
Wilson: You keep whittlin' that pin down, Tim, and that drill's gonna go visit the next crater over.
Tim: Just gotta hold the handles real tight, Wilson!

[exchange trigger=any.tim]
Tim: Say, neighbour, what if we double the voltage on the main hangar doors so they snap shut instantly?
Wilson: Nothin' wrong with a slow door, Tim. Gives a body time to keep their boots out of the seam.

[tim]
- What's cookin', captain? Put down that factory wrench, I've got three ideas to double our torque output right now!
- Tim here! Don't let the manual scare ya; every stock part is just an upgrade waiting for some real tools!
- You rang the right workshop, ace! Let's bore out those manifolds and see what this rig can really do!
- Just happened to be in the neighbourhood! Need a heavier weld-arc or a high-output blower strapped to that hull?
- Don't settle for factory specs, captain! A couple of extra coils and we'll have this whole grid humming like a wasp!
- Looking for extra kick? I was just eyein' your thruster feeds; with the right wrench, we can pull another ten percent!
- Workshop's open! If it doesn't move fast enough, we just haven't bolted a big enough motor to it yet, hotshot!

[idle]
- You push a conveyor tube too hard, neighbour, and it's liable to push back right through your bulkhead.
- A drill bit that never dulls usually ain't hittin' no rock. It's good to chew through a little iron now and then.
- Ain't no sense cursin' at a dead battery. Sun'll come back around the asteroid when it's good and ready.
- Reckon an engineer with two gyroscopes is cautious, but an engineer with twelve is fixin' to play spin the station.
- You can't rush an ingot through a cold refinery, neighbour. Heat takes time, just like seasonin' an old cast iron pan.
- Sometimes the best way to dodge an asteroid is just bein' somewhere else entirely when it comes driftin' through.
- Klang don't visit folks who tighten their rotor locks, neighbour. He mostly just drops in on the impatient ones.

[squabble]
- Now hold your horses, folks. No call to blow the seals off each other over a couple of misplaced iron plates.
- Well now, let's step back from the fence. Screamin' over the comms never pushed a kilogram of thrust yet.
- Easy there, neighbours. Even two docked ships gotta allow a little play in the merge blocks, or the struts snap.
- Ain't nobody winnin' an argument in a vacuum. Let's vent the steam before we burn a hole in the carpet.
- Quiet down the radios now. You're both right, you're both stubborn, and neither one of you's movin' the ore faster.
- Sounds to me like two roosters fightin' over who gets to crow at the solar panels. Let's get back to work.
- Now, now. Save that fire for the thrusters, friends. Station's too cramped for bad blood between good hands.



